{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"eilenberg-moore-displayed","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category"}]},"title_text":"The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category","kind":"note","taxon":null,"url":"eilenberg-moore-displayed.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"entry","attrs":[["entry","eilenberg-moore-displayed"],["kind","note"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Fix a monad "},{"Math":{"src":"lr(( T \\, eta \\, mu ))"}},{"Text":" on "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(C)"}},{"Text":". Its Eilenberg–Moore category arises in two displayed layers. The first layer is the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"algebras-displayed","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"displayed category of algebras"}]}},{"Text":" "},{"Math":{"src":"\"AlgStr\" lr(( T ))"}},{"Text":" of the underlying endofunctor."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The second layer, "},{"Math":{"src":"\"EMStr\" lr(( T ))"}},{"Text":", is displayed over the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"total-category","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"total category"}]}},{"Text":" "},{"Math":{"src":"\"Alg\" lr(( T ))"}},{"Text":". Over an algebra "},{"Math":{"src":"lr(( x \\, alpha ))"}},{"Text":" the displayed objects are the "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"propositions"}]},{"Text":" that "},{"Math":{"src":"alpha"}},{"Text":" satisfies the monad algebra laws:"}]},{"Math":{"src":"eta_x ⋆ alpha = sans(\"id\")_x wide mu_x ⋆ alpha = T alpha ⋆ alpha ."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The Eilenberg–Moore category is the total category of the tower:"}]},{"Math":{"src":"\"EM\" lr(( T )) = ∫ \"EMStr\" lr(( T )) ."}}]}}}]}}
